+## OpenStorm .170 immediate provider HTTP Kernels
+
+Literal providers registered on the returned application participate in initial
+HTTP Kernel ownership. Concrete register methods use shared class/trait source
+resolution; public bindings then singletons maps retain Laravel's ordering.
+Application aliases, duplicate registration and explicit force preserve object
+identity. Queued providers and boot callbacks remain outside the initial phase.
+Unmodeled bootstrap execution or escaped application values cannot establish a
+complete lifecycle; constructor expressions in register parameter defaults also
+remain incomplete. Provider and ancestor files must load only modeled declarations
+and data. Unused helper bodies remain separate. Unknown effects keep alternatives incomplete and cannot authorize checked edits.
+Contributed by @thinkycz.
+
 ## OpenStorm .163 stdio descriptor ownership
 
 **Isolated stdio startup on macOS.** The language server releases unrelated inherited streams before starting its workers, so another tool can finish reading its input while PHPantom stays running. Standard LSP input/output remain available. Contributed by @thinkycz.
